1615 0 obj
<<
/Title (Receives a 50Hz PWM signal from an external controller, which it processes internally to determine the target position of its output shaft. Unlike raw DC motors, it relies on a specific timing protocol where the duration of a high-voltage pulse dictates the precise angle of rotation. We can use a library like the Arduino Servo.h library that implements this strict timing and background refresh protocol. Like DC motor the servo actuator can have stall current problem.)
/Dest [21 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1598 0 R
/Prev 1614 0 R
/First 1621 0 R
/Last 1621 0 R
/Count -1
>>
